    {
      "id": "GR.pronoun-types",
      "track": "grammar",
      "prerequisites": [
        "GR.subject-object-pronouns"
      ],
      "ruleVersion": 1,
      "note": "Telling the five kinds of pronoun apart, which is what Alberta's one outcome for them actually asks (conventions.grade5.11, \"Distinguish between different types of pronouns used in a sentence\" — it names the class and lists no types). GR.reflexives, GR.relative, GR.interrogative, GR.demonstrative and GR.indefinite stay declared and empty: they are the same outcome cut five ways, and whether any one of them needs a pack of its own is a question the children's own answers can settle. Parent decision, 2026-09-19: build one pack now and split later if the evidence asks for it."
    },
